{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/867627-kiasyd-for-2nd-edition","id":867627,"title":"Kiasyd for 2nd Edition...","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-04-18T09:58:23-07:00","id":867627,"title":"Kiasyd for 2nd Edition...","content":"So, these are my favorite bloodline. I just think there is something about them - their history, their x-files strangeness, their flavor. <br /> <br /> I know there has been some attempts to recreate them for first edition and all of that. One of the attempts was to make Mythercia a bunch of devotions which Iiked but it still didn't fit exactly right. <br /> <br /> I definitely want to keep them more Fae origins then some of their other origins. So, I think it would be great to convert over their discipline version from the 2nd edition Storytellers handbook. The one where it resembled more fae magic like stone spikes and turn people to stone. <br /> <br /> Thoughts? Ideas?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;No live organism can continue for long to exist sanely under conditions of absolute reality; even larks and katydids are supposed, by some, to dream.&quot; - Shirley Jackson","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1227-shenron","name":"Shenron","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1227_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"193"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-18T10:16:37-07:00","id":867644,"title":"","content":"Personally, I never liked Mytherceria as a linear discipline, myself. Fae magic in owod was so much more open. And now, in 2nd edition CofD, Changelings have some more open magic again (Contracts are purchased individually, goblin vows and talecrafting are typical, etc). So I'd suggest trying to capture the feel of CofD Changelings in the discipline somehow, and to make it something more than just a 1-5 power chain.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/themes/stvault/images/affiliatebanner4.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Christopher%20Falco&amp;affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\">Storytellers' Vault supplements (WoD, CoD)</a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/FalconianP\" target=\"_blank\">My Patreon! (CofD bonuses include: Fae Sorcery/Technomancy for Vampires, Quick Conversion for Inferno, and more!)</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1130-falco1029","name":"falco1029","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1130_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1045"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-19T09:22:03-07:00","id":868486,"title":"","content":"Are you thinking along the lines of magic rituals? I don't really think they should just straight up copy powers from the Fae.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;No live organism can continue for long to exist sanely under conditions of absolute reality; even larks and katydids are supposed, by some, to dream.&quot; - Shirley Jackson","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1227-shenron","name":"Shenron","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1227_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"193"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-19T10:15:54-07:00","id":868533,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shenron</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/867627-kiasyd-for-2nd-edition?p=868486#post868486\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Are you thinking along the lines of magic rituals? I don't really think they should just straight up copy powers from the Fae.</div> </div> </div> </div>Straight up copying is probably a bad idea, I agree, but I don't think it should be an entirely linear thing. I also don't think it should work like blood sorcery.<br /> <br /> I guess what I'd suggest, then, is something along the lines of a bloodline 'discipline' that gives you access to 'cantrips', which are spells that are sort of like contracts, coming from aspects of reality in a changelingy way, and instantaneous-use like a lot of disciplines are (I can't see them ever really being disciplines). Probably slightly weaker than equivalent level blood sorcery rituals, but more showy and obviously magical and fae-like. Maybe include in their Bloodline Gift that they have some way to harness Glamour, and use that instead of Vitae solely for that 'discipline'? Dunno, mostly spitballing here.<br /> <br /> EDIT: A second idea is to, again, give them a way to use Glamour, but instead of giving them a new discipline, if they use Glamour INSTEAD of Vitae in their existing disciplines, it creates new, more fae-like effects. Obfuscate might curl shadows around you instead of making you project a mental 'ignore me', Dominate 1 might physically cause the ground to reach up and hold someone in place if you command them to 'stay still', etc. Granted, that requires more ST intervention.<br /> <br /> In either case, I'd make seeing past the mask innate to them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/themes/stvault/images/affiliatebanner4.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Christopher%20Falco&amp;affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\">Storytellers' Vault supplements (WoD, CoD)</a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/FalconianP\" target=\"_blank\">My Patreon! (CofD bonuses include: Fae Sorcery/Technomancy for Vampires, Quick Conversion for Inferno, and more!)</a>","edited":{"userid":1130,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1130-falco1029","user":"falco1029","date":". 04-19-2016, 01:33 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1130-falco1029","name":"falco1029","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1130_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1045"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}